{"kind":"nesy.translation/1","eventId":"translation","label":"inferred","data":{"text":"An object's bounding box spans rows 10 to 14 and columns 3 to 9. Its click point is its centroid clamped into the bounding box, one coordinate at a time. The centroid is at row 16 and column 6. So the click point's row is 16.","formula":"; \"An object's bounding box spans rows 10 to 14 and columns 3 to 9.\"\n(declare-const bbox_row_min Int)\n(declare-const bbox_row_max Int)\n(declare-const bbox_col_min Int)\n(declare-const bbox_col_max Int)\n(assert (= bbox_row_min 10))\n(assert (= bbox_row_max 14))\n(assert (= bbox_col_min 3))\n(assert (= bbox_col_max 9))\n\n; \"Its click point is its centroid clamped into the bounding box, one coordinate at a time.\"\n(declare-const centroid_row Int)\n(declare-const centroid_col Int)\n(assert (= centroid_row 16))\n(assert (= centroid_col 6))\n\n; \"The centroid is at row 16 and column 6. So the click point's row is 16.\"\n(declare-const click_row Int)\n(assert (>= click_row bbox_row_min))\n(assert (<= click_row bbox_row_max))\n(assert (= click_row centroid_row))","assertions":[{"formula":"(assert (= bbox_row_min 10))","quote":"An object's bounding box spans rows 10 to 14 and columns 3 to 9.","span":[0,63],"departures":[{"check":"numbers","detail":"The words give 10, 14, 3, 9; the assertion has 10."}]},{"formula":"(assert (= bbox_row_max 14))","quote":null,"span":null,"departures":[{"check":"quote","detail":"No comment says which words of the problem this assertion encodes."}]},{"formula":"(assert (= bbox_col_min 3))","quote":null,"span":null,"departures":[{"check":"quote","detail":"No comment says which words of the problem this assertion encodes."}]},{"formula":"(assert (= bbox_col_max 9))","quote":null,"span":null,"departures":[{"check":"quote","detail":"No comment says which words of the problem this assertion encodes."}]},{"formula":"(assert (= centroid_row 16))","quote":"Its click point is its centroid clamped into the bounding box, one coordinate at a time.","span":[65,152],"departures":[{"check":"numbers","detail":"The words give 1; the assertion has 16."}]},{"formula":"(assert (= centroid_col 6))","quote":null,"span":null,"departures":[{"check":"quote","detail":"No comment says which words of the problem this assertion encodes."}]},{"formula":"(assert (>= click_row bbox_row_min))","quote":"The centroid is at row 16 and column 6. So the click point's row is 16.","span":[154,224],"departures":[{"check":"numbers","detail":"The words give 16, 16, 6; the assertion has none."}]},{"formula":"(assert (<= click_row bbox_row_max))","quote":null,"span":null,"departures":[{"check":"quote","detail":"No comment says which words of the problem this assertion encodes."}]},{"formula":"(assert (= click_row centroid_row))","quote":null,"span":null,"departures":[{"check":"quote","detail":"No comment says which words of the problem this assertion encodes."}]}],"unencoded":[],"rules":["Each assertion's comment quotes words that are in the problem, ignoring case and spacing.","The numbers in the quoted words, as digits or as words up to twelve, are the numbers in the assertion.","Where the quoted words name a comparison (above, at least, younger than…), the assertion makes that comparison, read with the symbol on the left.","Every sentence of the problem is quoted by some assertion."],"limitations":"The checks read words, not meaning. They do not check which side of a comparison each symbol is on, negation in the words, or units, so a wrong formula can pass. An equivalent rewriting, such as x > 17 for at least 18, is flagged. The quotes are the model's own claim about what each assertion encodes."}}
